# Keep the build context small without breaking the build.
#
# vendor/ is deliberately NOT listed here, and that is the whole reason this
# file is written by hand rather than generated. The image is built with
# -mod=vendor on a host that may have no network, so the vendored dependencies
# must travel in the context. Excluding vendor/ — which is what a "clean"
# dockerignore template would do, on the assumption that the build fetches its
# own modules — turns the build into a failure.
#
# Nothing under internal/seed/documents/ may be excluded either, for a different
# reason: those files are compiled into the binary with //go:embed, so a missing
# one fails the build with "no matching files found" rather than failing at
# runtime. This is why there is no blanket *.md rule below.

.git
.gitignore

# Real credentials live here, and the image must never carry them: the
# application reads them from the environment at run time.
.env
.env.*

# Generated on the VM by Ansible, mounted into the nginx container at run time.
certs/

# Mounted into the nginx container at run time and not needed to build the Go
# binary.
nginx/
docker-compose.yml

*.log
